# Dependencies
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Build outputs
frontend/dist/

# NOTE: backend/data/processed/models/*.{bin,pkl,npy,npz} used to be excluded
# here on a blanket "don't commit binary ML artifacts" rule. That meant the
# trained FAISS index / embeddings / TF-IDF / CF factors never reached
# GitHub, so the deployed backend always ran with cf_engine/cbf_engine
# "degraded" (see /health) — not a ranking bug, just missing files. They're
# ~20MB total and there's no retraining pipeline wired into deployment (see
# backend/app/tasks/celery_tasks.py), so shipping the already-trained
# artifacts in git is the pragmatic choice: verified 2026-09-12 that they
# still match the live product catalogue (ids 0-5059, 5060 rows) and load
# cleanly. If a real training pipeline is added later, re-exclude these and
# have that pipeline publish artifacts to deployment instead.

# NEVER commit secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.env
!.env.example

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Test cache
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
